> **When to follow this**: any time you bump `Chart.yaml`'s `version`/`appVersion`
> or `rivolt-infra/apps/rivolt/app.yaml`'s `chart.version`. The chart version
> is a git tag that must be created and pushed; without step 3 ArgoCD fails
> with `unable to resolve 'v0.X.Y' to a commit SHA`.

# Ship-it Process

When the user says "ship it" (or asks to release / deploy), run these steps **in order**:

## 1. Determine the next version
```
git log --oneline -1   # read the last vX.Y.Z to derive the next patch
```

## 2. Bump `deploy/helm/rivolt/Chart.yaml`
Both fields must be updated together — they must equal the new git tag:
```yaml
version: 0.8.Y        # patch-bumps in sync with appVersion
appVersion: "0.X.Y"   # pod image tag — MUST match the git tag
```

## 3. Commit, tag & push in `rivolt`
```
git add <changed files> deploy/helm/rivolt/Chart.yaml
git commit -m "v0.X.Y: <short summary>"
git tag v0.X.Y
git push origin main
git push origin v0.X.Y
```
Push the tag explicitly — `--follow-tags` only pushes annotated tags,
and we create lightweight tags, so the tag must be pushed separately.
CI publishes `ghcr.io/apohor/rivolt:0.X.Y` on tag push only — wait
for the Actions run to go green before bumping infra.

## 4. Bump the infra chart in `rivolt-infra`
Push immediately after step 3 — no need to wait for CI. ArgoCD will
attempt to pull the image and retry automatically until it lands.
```
# in rivolt-infra:
# apps/rivolt/app.yaml → chart.version: v0.X.Y
git add apps/rivolt/app.yaml
git commit -m "rivolt: bump to v0.X.Y"
git push
```

## Checklist
- [ ] `Chart.yaml` `version` + `appVersion` bumped
- [ ] `git push origin main && git push origin vX.Y.Z` done
- [ ] `rivolt-infra` `app.yaml` bumped & pushed
- [ ] ArgoCD synced, pod on new version (`kubectl -n rivolt get pods`)
